# mentorOS — Design System

Source: coda.io design tokens + mentorOS brand layer.  
Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` (`@theme { ... }`).

---

## Design philosophy (Coda-inspired)

The mentorOS shell follows Coda visual language:

- Crisp white canvas with warm **amber-glow** sections for hero and footer
- Strong **Montserrat 700** display headlines with tight negative letter-spacing
- **Inter** for all body, navigation, and UI text
- **Obsidian (#000000)** for primary CTAs — not blue
- Monochrome base palette with product-specific color accents only on product elements
- Generous spacing — Coda uses 113px between sections
- Cards use subtle shadow, NOT heavy borders
- Buttons are always **8px border-radius** (`rounded-md`) — never pill, never sharp (shell)

---

## Color rules

### Shell and layout colors — use for all non-product UI

| Token | Class | Hex |
|-------|-------|-----|
| Page background | `bg-white-canvas` | #ffffff |
| Hero/footer warm | `bg-amber-glow` | #fff6ec |
| Primary text | `text-midnight-ink` | #212121 |
| Muted body | `text-slate-text` | #666666 |
| Helper text | `text-ash-text` | #8e8e8e |
| Subtle borders | `border-soft-gray` | #e0e0e0 |
| Primary CTA bg | `bg-obsidian` | #000000 |
| CTA text | `text-white-canvas` | #ffffff |
| Secondary btn | `text-warm-gray` | #444444 |
| Accent highlight | `text-sunset-orange` | #ee5a29 (sparingly) |

### Product accent colors — ONLY on product cards and module UI

**PMP Thinking Coach:**
- Primary `#2563EB` → `text-pmp-primary`
- Accent `#7C3AED` → `text-pmp-accent`
- Surface `#EEF2FF` → `bg-pmp-surface`
- Gradient → `bg-gradient-pmp` (135deg #2563EB → #7C3AED)

**AskBetter:** `askbetter-primary`, `askbetter-accent`, `askbetter-surface`, `bg-gradient-askbetter`

**NextUp:** `nextup`, `nextup-purple`, `nextup-surface`, `bg-gradient-nextup`

**BidMentor:** `bidmentor`, `bidmentor-primary`, `bidmentor-surface`, `bg-gradient-bidmentor`

### Do NOT

- Use blue as primary CTA on shell — use `bg-obsidian`
- Use product colors in navbar, footer, or page backgrounds (except product module interiors)
- Hardcode hex in JSX when a token exists — prefer Tailwind classes
- **Exception:** PDF/html2canvas export surfaces in PMP use explicit hex (`#FFFFFF`, `#2563EB`) to avoid `oklab` parse errors

