## Hero landing within a product page

**Reference:** `InputScreen.tsx`

PMP landing is a **hero inside `/pmp`**, not the marketing homepage.

- Full-width **amber-glow** background on module (`min-h-[calc(100vh-56px)]`)
- Hero typography + dual CTAs (`Khám phá 2 chế độ học`, `Tải đề lên`)
- Feature cards section (`featureCardsRef`) — scroll target for "Câu hỏi mới"
- Unified input box below cards (`inputBoxRef`) — scroll target for upload
- **Does not replace** shell navbar — navbar stays fixed above (`Navbar.tsx`)
- On desktop: sidebar replaces `PMPHeader` (`lg:hidden` on header)

---

## Navbar scroll behavior

**Reference:** `src/components/layout/Navbar.tsx`

| Behavior | Implementation |
|----------|----------------|
| Scroll down | Hide: `-translate-y-full` |
| Scroll up | Show: `translate-y-0` |
| At top (`scrollY < 10`) | Always visible |
| Transition | `transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out` only |
| Drawer open | Never hide (`isOpen` early return) |
| PMP transparent top | `pathname === '/pmp' && !scrolled` → `bg-transparent` |
| PMP scrolled | `bg-amber-glow border-[#E8D5BC]` |
| Home | `bg-amber-glow` |

Use `lastScrollY` ref (not state) to avoid re-renders on every scroll. Passive scroll listener.

